P26b is finished and ticked in `tasks.md`. Typecheck and lint are clean, `pnpm test` passes 295/295, and every e2e spec related to the task passes after a fresh build. No visual snapshots changed.

The previous session had already done almost all of the work: warm paper background `#F6F3EE` with warmer ink and hairlines, the self-hosted Instrument Serif and JetBrains Mono fonts, the italic accent word in Latin locales only, the larger landing headline, the mono "Sample lots" label with its ember dot, mono lot and wafer IDs, and the e2e colour updates. Two problems were left:

- **Verdict headline shrank in English.** It dropped from 48 px to 40 px. The serif accent's letter boxes stick out of their line by about 7 px, so the height check thought the headline had more than two lines. The check in `VerdictHero.tsx` now measures the actual line height (`clientHeight`) instead of `scrollHeight`, and it stays at 48 px.
- **Flaky test for Chinese, Japanese and Korean.** The page loads in English first and switches language after it starts. The test in `editorial-p26b.spec.ts` sometimes counted the English accent word before the switch, so it now waits for the language change.

Choices I made where premium.md gives no value, all recorded in `logs/progress.md`:

- The sunken fill, nav bar material and sheet backdrop keep their old cool grey values, and dark-theme text stays as it was.
- The landing footer line now sits below the 900 px fold, because the 72 px section gaps push it down. The landing e2e test only requires the content above the footer to fit on screen.
- Two items that A48 asks for in mono can't be done yet. The coordinate labels around the hero wafer and the "Example result" label don't exist until P26a builds them; they should use `.type-mono-note`. The magnifier's die coordinates are already in mono; the rest of the magnifier rework belongs to its own task.

